
{% comment %} spell:words autolyse {% endcomment %}

<section class="hero" id="top-header-block">
  <h1>{{ site.title }}</h1>
  <p class="subtitle-line narrow-top-margin">{{ site.pronunciation }}</p>
  {% include icon.liquid %}
  <p class="tagline">{{ site.tagline }}</p>
  <p class="description">
    Offline-first baking, shopping lists, and pantry inventory app with allergen-aware substitutions.
    Built by an engineer who deals with allergies personally every day.
  </p>
  <p class="pill pill-badge coming-soon">Coming soon</p>
  {% comment %}
  <a class="pill pill-button pill-block notify-link" href="{{ "/get_notified/" | relative_url }}">Get notified when we launch</a>
  {% endcomment %}
</section>

<h2 class="section-heading">What is Bakelorium</h2>

<div class="pillars" id="what-is-bakelorium">

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3 class="heading">Recipes</h3>
    <p>Share any way you want.</p>
    <p>Your recipes, your way.</p>
    <p>It's not just for baking!</p>
  </article>

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3 class="heading">Pantry</h3>
    <p>Inventory tracking at home.</p>
    <p>Barcode scanning.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3 class="heading">Shopping lists</h3>
    <p>For when you stop at the store.</p>
    <p>Add to shopping list from Recipes.</p>
    <p>Show inventory numbers from pantry.</p>
  </article>

</div>

<p class="section-body">And more. We can't just give away all our secrets.</p>

{% include platforms.liquid %}

<h2 class="section-heading">In your kitchen</h2>

<div class="pillars">

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3>Dietary Restrictions</h3>
    <p>Allergies.</p>
    <p>Preferences.</p>
    <p>Ingredient substitutions in recipe.</p>
    <p>Known allergens in recipe ingredients are shown.</p>
    <p>Each recipe lists which common allergens appear in its ingredients and where a known swap exists.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3>Recipes that scale with you</h3>
    <p>Change the servings and watch weights recalculate.</p>
    <p>Baker's percentages for your cooks.</p>
    <p>Metric or Imperial.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3>Baking science, built in</h3>
    <p>Inline glossary for terms like autolyse or lamination.</p>
    <p>Learn the why, not just the steps.</p>
    <p>Step-level notes explain what gluten, leavening, and temperature are actually doing.</p>
  </article>

</div>

<h2 class="section-heading">On your terms</h2>

<div class="pillars">

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3>Works without our cloud servers</h3>
    <p>No account. No email. No signup. No login. Open the app and start making.</p>
    <p>Designed to work without an internet connection, in the kitchen or on the go.</p>
    <p>The app doesn't need our servers to work.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3>Share recipes and sync lists phone-to-phone</h3>
    <p>QR code scan-to-import between two phones, no account or cloud round-trip.</p>
    <p>Recipes can be shared like any file.</p>
    <p>Our cloud server API is a convenience, not a requirement.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="pillar">
    <h3>No vendor lock-in</h3>

    <p>No AI features inside the app to pull your focus while you cook.</p>

    <p>No account, no signup required.</p>
    <p>No email, no login, nothing to remember.</p>
    <p>No subscriptions.</p>
    <p>No paid tiers.</p>
    <p>No features that expire.</p>

  </article>

</div>

<h2 class="section-body">Open the app and start baking.</h2>

<section class="info-band" id="you-own-your-data">
  <h2 class="band-heading">You own your data</h2>
  <p class="muted-text">Your recipes export as plain text files you can read without this app.</p>
  <ul class="tag-list center">
    <li class="tag">BakeBundle</li>
    <li class="tag">Markdown</li>
    <li class="tag">JSON-LD schema.org/Recipe</li>
    <li class="tag">Cooklang</li>
    <li class="tag">PDF</li>
    <li class="tag">Print</li>
  </ul>
</section>

{% include authors.liquid  %}

<section class="info-band" id="about-the-app">
  <h2 class="band-heading">More about the app</h2>
  <p class="muted-text">Follow along, see the code, or say hello.</p>
  <ul class="link-row center">
    <li><a class="pill pill-link" href="https://github.com/Bakelorium">Bakelorium on GitHub</a></li>
    {% comment %}
    <li><a class="pill pill-link" href="https://discord.gg/QxKygP3C5U">Join the Discord</a></li>
    {% endcomment %}
    <li><a class="pill pill-link"  href="{{ "/about/" | relative_url }}">More about Bakelorium</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>

{% comment %}
<p class="feedback-link"><a href="{{ "/feedback/" | relative_url }}">Have feedback or a question? Get in touch.</a></p>
{% endcomment %}
